    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Property Team Lappin Estates take great pleasure in presenting “Roker”, a superb detached residence offering an enviable lifestyle in one of Dublin’s most sought-after coastal locations. Perfectly situated close to Howth Village and Harbour, this property is ideal for those who appreciate scenic beauty, outdoor pursuits, and a vibrant community atmosphere.\r\nHowth beautifully retains its historic village character while offering a sophisticated lifestyle. Residents can enjoy local boutiques, excellent seafood restaurants, cozy pubs, a local library, schools, and essential amenities. For outdoor enthusiasts, the famous scenic Cliff Walks and the Summit are just up the hill, while the immediate area boasts exceptional clubs catering to sailing, golf, and numerous other sporting disciplines.\r\nCommuting is effortless with a regular bus service passing right by your front door. The nearby Howth DART station provides rapid, reliable transport links directly into Dublin City Centre and beyond.\r\nThe accommodation briefly comprises entrance hall, living/ dining room, kitchen, extended breakfast room, study/playroom, guest w.c and utility room, 4 bedrooms, 2 en-suites and a family bathroom. Outside there is a large front garden laid in lawn, with a large driveway. \r\nThe back garden has a detached garage which has potential to be converted (subject to planning).\r\nViewing is very highly recommended!"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall\t4.90m x 3.10m\tTiled floor, recessed lights, attic trap door and under stairs storage.\r\n\r\nGuest WC\t\tWC, whb and tiled floor.\r\n\r\nUtility Room\t\tPlumbed for washing machine.\r\n\r\nStudy/Playroom\t3.70 x 2.70m\t\r\n\r\nLiving/Dining Room\t9.30m x 3.80m\tWooden flooring, open fireplace and coved ceiling.\r\n\r\nKitchen\t3.80m x 3.00\tFitted wall and floor units, tiled floor and free standing range gas cooker.\r\n\r\nExtended Breakfast Room\t4.20m x 3.30m  Double doors to rear garden and tiled floor.\r\n\r\nBedroom 4)\t4.20m x 3.10m\tFitted shelving and presses, coved ceiling and dado rail.\r\n\r\nLanding\t\tHot press\r\n\r\nBedroom 1)\t4.00m x 4.00\tFitted wardrobes.  Large double room.\r\n\r\nWalk in Wardrobe\t1.90m x 1.70m\t\r\n\r\nEn-Suite\t2.10m x 1.80m\tShower unit, WC, whb, tiled walls and floor.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2)\t3.40m x 3.20m\t\r\n\r\nBathroom\t2.50m x 2.00m\tBath, shower, WC, whb. Tiled floor and walls\r\n\r\nBedroom 3)\t4.30m x 3.80m\tFitted wardrobes\r\n\r\nEnsuite\t\tShower, WC, whb. Tiled floor and walls.\r\n\r\nDetached Garage\t4.40m x 3.60m\tWith potential to develop subject to Planning Permission.\r\n\r\nOutside\t\tThere is a large garden to the front that is laid in lawn and provides lots of off street parking.  The rear garden is laid in lawn with a decking and patio area.  There is side pedestrian access from the front garden to the back garden.  The detached garage offers potential to convert (subject to planning and regulations)."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Detached 4 bedroom dormer bungalow\r\nG.F.C.H. Combi boiler c 4 yrs old\r\nLarge front garden and driveway\r\nDetached garage with potential to develop.\r\n2 en-suites\r\nHarwood double glazed windows\r\nGuest downstairs WC\r\nMain bathroom upstairs\r\nWell serviced by public transport, buses and DART\r\nMagnificent coastal cliff walks on the doorstep\r\nHowth Village is a vibrant fishing village with an abundance of shops, restaurants, pubs, clubs, recreational facilities and schools"
      },
